phpstan.neon

/public/build
/storage/pail
.env.backup
.env.production
.phpactor.json
auth.json

# Workbench (the development Laravel app in workbench/)
#
# The skeleton itself is committed so every contributor gets the same dev app.
# Only its runtime output is ignored: synced storage, the sqlite database and
# published assets are all regenerated by `composer build`.
#
# No trailing slash on the first two, deliberately: `testbench serve` creates
# them as symlinks into the skeleton under vendor/, and a pattern ending in `/`
# matches directories only — so the slash version let an untracked symlink
# through for anyone who served the application.
/workbench/storage
/workbench/public
/workbench/database/*.sqlite
#
# And what `spec:build` emits, for the same reason any project ignores its build
# output. The Workbench exists to model a real consumer application, so it is
# configured the way one would be: the contract is committed, what the contract
# produces is not. `composer build` regenerates it, and the build is wired into
# that step rather than left for somebody to remember.
/workbench/app/Http/Generated

